# Robinhood Chain launches: the launch contracts in contracts/curve-launch-evm on Robinhood Chain — every coin a Uniswap v4
# pool from its first block, liquidity locked. Append what you need to /etc/launchpad.env, then restart launchpad. Never
# commit or package real values.

# Master switch. Off: every /api/launchpad/robinhood route answers 503, the launch page offers Solana only,
# and the worker never starts.
LAUNCHPAD_ROBINHOOD_LAUNCH_ENABLED=1

# The contracts, as printed by the deploy script (docs/ROBINHOOD.md). All six are required.
LAUNCHPAD_RH_LAUNCH_FACTORY=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
LAUNCHPAD_RH_FEE_ESCROW=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
LAUNCHPAD_RH_LAUNCH_LOCKER=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
LAUNCHPAD_RH_RULE_ENGINE=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
LAUNCHPAD_RH_SWAP_ROUTER=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
LAUNCHPAD_RH_PAYOUTS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
# The chain's Uniswap v4 PoolManager (the official deployment; the default is the one the deploy script used).
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_POOL_MANAGER=0x8366a39CC670B4001A1121B8F6A443A643e40951

# Where the platform share is swept (an address you control on Robinhood Chain). Without it the platform wallet
# claims from the escrow and keeps what it claims; sweeps start when the treasury is set.
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_TREASURY=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# The chain's RPC. The public endpoint (the default) is rate-limited and meant for wallets and testing: a live host
# needs a dedicated endpoint (Chainstack, Alchemy, QuickNode, dRPC and Validation Cloud serve chain 4663; the host
# needs eth_getLogs). The endpoint URL carries your key: it lives only here.
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_RPC_URL=https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com
# Requests per second the host allows itself: 15 on the public endpoint, 50 on a dedicated one unless set;
# keep a margin under the provider's ceiling (a Chainstack Growth plan allows 250: 100 to 200 is right).
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_RPC_RPS=100

# Optional locations (defaults shown). Include both in your backups.
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_DB_PATH=/opt/launchpad/data/robinhood-launch/robinhood-launch.sqlite
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_BACKUP_DIR=/opt/launchpad/data/robinhood-launch/backups

# The USD value at which a Holders / Diamond Hands coin pays its holders (default 100; 1 to 1,000,000).
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_HOLDER_PAYOUT_USD=100

# A fixed ETH price in USD, only when the chain's own Uniswap pools cannot be read for it (tests, outages).
# LAUNCHPAD_RH_ETH_USD=4000

# Already part of a normal install and required here:
#   LAUNCHPAD_PUBLIC_URL      https address; coin metadata is served from it
#   the encrypted host store (LAUNCHPAD_MASTER_KEY_FILE): the per-coin and host wallets live in it
